{
  "cell": "prompt-lookup-speculation (INK2_SPEC)",
  "question": "does the zero-weight drafter (the context's own n-grams) pay in Inkling-2's CUDA chain, and is its text the same as plain decoding?",
  "design": "spec_lookup drafts up to INK2_SPEC_DRAFTS tokens from the token history; one forward of S = drafts + 1 rows verifies them (row r fed at pos + r, its argmax the token at pos + r + 1); the chain computes every row's final norm, head and argmax on the card (cc_pick_rows) and the loop reads back only the rows the picks agree with; on a rejection the convolution banks go back to the host copy taken before the verify and the accepted prefix is fed again in one forward, K/V rows being positional. Depth is spec_draft.h's gate (measured acceptance by position, measured T(n), fitted rho); INK2_SPEC_GATE=0 drafts every proposal.",
