  "notes": [
    "The bench prompts are the repetitive filler of bench/make_prompts.py, so the lookup fires on nearly every step: these are the lookup drafter's best case, not free text.",
    "The gate's cost model does not price the replay a rejection costs (one forward of `keep` rows): a rejection at the first draft pays T(S) + T(1) for one token. On these prompts 5-6% of drafts are rejected so it does not show; on free text the acceptance EMA is what stops the drafting.",
    "The 64K decode is 32 tokens, so the gate has 10 verifies to learn from: 2.07 tokens a forward against 4.50 at depth 4 with the gate off on the 721 cell.",
    "The 721-token cell is the noisy one: the same configuration measured 42.21 and 48.34 in two back-to-back pairs (COLI_CUDA_CHAIN_MOE makes no difference there: 0 of 24 layers' experts run in the frame either way) and 48.08 against 34.55 on the run before the final rebuild, so read that cell as +20% to +40%."
  ]
